      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Upboting because I do think there needs to be improvements to this system, even if I disagree with quite a few of your suggestions for it. \n\nDecline notifications are an extremely bad idea that would promote toxicity. There's a reason why not many services do this: No one wants to be told they were rejected.  At the risk of sounding bad, there's a few people on my friendslist that I can't remove without paying consequences, and I know they'd have a heyday over me declining them.  I think this would create a social risk for many users.\n\nI'm not entirely sure if a timer would help that much, but it'd have a less psychologically impactful effect than a decline notification for sure. I wouldn't mind a timer for the person who received the invite/request though, there's been many times that I've ran out of time before accepting. \n\nI definitely agree that invite requests being passed to the instance owner would be nice, especially if it can still be passed along to them without the person requesting knowing who they are. \n\nLogistically, I think a decline reason(if such a thing were implemented) would be cumbersome and annoying for most users.\n\nI'm not too certain how well an invite cancel button would actually work in function or logistically. Invites tend to be too quick for that, and(like my opinion on decline notifications), could have negative sociological impacts.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
