      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b2c4eb538839d3a41d1ff26|full_name}: fair arguments :) Most of the points listed above in my post were from a discussion on a live stream so there were a lot of ideas thrown around. I tried to list all the ones i could remember as suggestions. \n\nThe biggest criticisms are the invites not being passed to the instance owner and there not being any kind of feedback from an invite request, so many end up waiting for a long time for a potential invite whereas knowing that the invite timed out or was declined lets you move on to something else.\n\nI would like to hope people can avoid getting into social situations where they are forced to keep someone as a friend or let them join every request. No one should have that kind of power over anyone but I'm aware that it does happen which really sucks. Honestly if paying consequences means that some \"friends\" will leave you because you aren't friends with person A, then its probably best you look for a new group and not hang out with people following Person A.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
