  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The invite system needs to be priorisited a bit. Some problems with the invite system right now that should be fixed asap:\n\n- you have no idea whats going on with your invite. you're left in the dark not knowing if the invite expired , declined etc  \n\none way to improve this, is show a timer on the invite you sent so you can see it expired or if it was declined before time ran out.\n\nThe same should happen once you have accepted an invite and are waiting for the requester to accept the invite you accepted.\n\nRight now, having to send an invite and waiting indefinitely is a big problem and kills the experience quite a bit. No one wants to sit around for an hour wondering why they haven't had any invites back or something.\n\n- Requesting invite off someone who is in an invite only world owned by someone else\n\nThis is super annoying because the invite never gets passed on to the instance owner. So the requester is just left in the dark thinking their friend is ignoring them, when that friend is unable to invite them.\n\n- Give a way for people to give a reason for declining an invite\n\nLike the way the status works, a quick message like \"sorry, testing for bugs in world, can't invite\" or \"sorry, I'm not allowed to invite\"\n\nOr just give players the option to use whats in their status as the reason.\n\n- Can't cancel an invite\n\nWould help when you send an invite by mistake\n \nThese are just some of the fustrations from the community. Feel free to add more in the comments too.",
